    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Rewrite as directed (10×1=10):\n(a) Mother made a cake yesterday. (Passive)\n(b) He said to me, “Where is the post office?” (Indirect speech)\n(c) His bravery was admired. (Active)\n(d) The boys said, “Hurrah, we have won the match!” (Indirect speech)\n(e) We will win or die. (Compound to complex)\n(f) Elon Musk is the richest person in the world. (Superlative to comparative)\n(g) Aizawl is a more populous city than Lunglei. (Comparative to positive)\n(h) I raided her closet. There were plenty of bags. They were all designer bags. The bags were all white in colour. (Combine)\n(i) Why waste money here? (Interrogative to assertive)\n(j) These oranges are sour. (Assertive to negative)",
    "explanation": "Examples: (a) A cake was made by Mother yesterday. (b) He asked me where the post office was. (c) People admired his bravery. (d) The boys exclaimed with joy that they had won the match. (e) If we do not win, we will die. (f) Elon Musk is richer than any other person in the world. (This is a grammatical transformation of the printed claim.) (g) Lunglei is not as populous as Aizawl. (h) I raided her closet, which contained plenty of white designer bags. (i) It is pointless to waste money here. (j) These oranges are not sweet. The last is a conventional classroom transformation; not sweet is not a strict logical synonym of sour.",
    "sourceReview": false,
    "sourceNote": "",
    "source": "Assistant Sub-Inspector of Police (Ministerial) · November 2024",
    "year": 2024,
    "sourceHref": "/papers/group-b/asi-2024-p1.pdf#page=3"
