    "type": "descriptive",
    "questionNumber": "3",
    "subject": "english",
    "studySection": "english",
    "topic": "written",
    "topicLabel": "General English · written",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Read the passage and answer all ten questions below. (Questions (a)–(e) on page 2 carry 1 mark each; questions (f)–(j) on page 3 carry 2 marks each.)\n\nExercise is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle. It helps improve cardiovascular health, strengthens muscles, and boosts the immune system. Regular physical activity also reduces the risk of chronic diseases such as heart disease, diabetes, and obesity. Additionally, exercise plays a crucial role in mental well-being by reducing stress, anxiety, and depression.\n\nThere are different types of exercises, including aerobic exercises like running and swimming, strength training like weightlifting, and flexibility exercises such as yoga and stretching. A combination of these exercises ensures overall fitness and health. Experts recommend at least 30 minutes of moderate exercise per day to maintain good health.\n\nThe lack of physical activity has become a major concern, especially with modern lifestyles that involve sitting for long hours. Many people spend excessive time on screens, leading to a sedentary lifestyle. This can result in weight gain, muscle weakness, and poor cardiovascular health. To stay active, individuals can take small steps such as walking instead of driving, using stairs instead of elevators, and participating in sports or outdoor activities.\n\nGovernments and health organizations promote exercise through awareness campaigns, fitness programs, and policies that encourage active lifestyles. Schools also play a key role by including physical education in their curriculum. Exercise is not just about fitness—it is a way to enhance the quality of life and increase life expectancy.\n\n(a) ______ exercise includes activities like running and swimming.\n(b) A sedentary lifestyle can lead to ______ gain.\n(c) Give a synonym of “guarantee” (the question says “second paragraph”).\n(d) Give an antonym of “diminish” (the question says “fourth paragraph”).\n(e) Give one way in which a school can promote physical activity.\n(f) What flexibility exercises are mentioned in the passage?\n(g) Why is exercise important for overall health?\n(h) How does exercise contribute to mental well-being?\n(i) How can individuals include more physical activity in their daily routine?\n(j) What role do governments and health organizations play in promoting exercise?",
    "answers": ["aerobic", "weight"],
    "explanation": "Answer guide: (a) aerobic; (b) weight; (c) ensure(s), which appears in the second paragraph and means to make certain; (d) increase, the antonym of “diminish” used in the fourth paragraph. (e) include physical education in the curriculum; (f) yoga and stretching; (g) it improves cardiovascular health, strengthens muscles, boosts immunity and lowers chronic-disease risk; (h) it reduces stress, anxiety and depression; (i) walk instead of driving, use stairs, or take part in sports/outdoor activities; (j) run awareness campaigns and fitness programs and adopt policies encouraging active lifestyles.",
    "sourceReview": false,
    "sourceNote": "",
    "source": "Sub-Inspector FCS&CA / Receptionist H&FW · May 2025",
    "year": 2025,
    "sourceHref": "/papers/group-b/si-fcs-2025-p1.pdf#page=2"
