    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Write a précis of the following passage in about one third of its original length:        (10×1=10)\n            The cinema is an outstanding wonder of this modern age. Apart from the great pleasure it gives\n     us as a means of entertainment, it is in many ways an education itself, and no regular patron of the\n     cinema can be called illiterate. The cinema is also a very valuable asset to educationists. The film\n     companies, from time to time, produce historical pictures and their pictures are of great importance\n     to the teacher of history. A couple of hours spent in viewing some of historical personages dressed in\n     the proper dress of that period can gain a much better idea of the play than a whole week’s browsing\n     in a history text book. Even some of Shakespeare’s dramas and comedies have been filmed and we\n     thereby gain a much better idea of the play than would be possible from a casual reading of it.\n           But of the far greater importance is the use of the film in the teaching of science and industry.\n     There are educational film companies which devote their time to the filming of the habits and customs\n     of animals, insects, fishes, germs and numerous other branches of scientific life. We can see the\n     hatching of the egg of fish and their gradual development into large fishes; we can watch the unceasing\n     activity of many kinds of germs and their effect on water, milk or blood. We can watch the opening\n     and closing of flowers and leaves and the growth of grass and weeds. All these actions and movements\n     are greatly magnified on the screen. Such pictures are intensely interesting and are a great help to the\n     cause of education.",
    "explanation": "Suggested title: Cinema as an Educational Aid. In about one third of the passage’s length, explain that films both entertain and teach, make history and literature vivid, and reveal scientific processes through magnified images. Preserve the balance of the two paragraphs and do not add examples absent from the source.",
