    "explanation": "Suggested forms: (a) is; (b) was; (c) are is idiomatic with plural “those” (is is also grammatical under a singular interpretation of “none”); (d) has; (e) is; (f) have; (g) are; (h) are under the ordinary reading of two rewards; (i) loves; (j) have. “Honour and glory” can be construed as one combined idea, so (h) is context-sensitive.",
