    "question": "Write a précis of the following passage by reducing it to one third of its length (10 marks):\n\nReading is one of the most valuable habits a person can develop. It opens up new worlds, ideas, and perspectives, enriching the mind and imagination. Through books, articles, and other written materials, people gain knowledge about history, science, culture, and human behaviour. Reading also improves language skills, vocabulary, and critical thinking. It encourages curiosity and creativity, allowing individuals to explore concepts beyond their immediate experiences. Furthermore, reading can be a source of relaxation and stress relief, offering an escape from the pressures of daily life. In a world full of distractions, dedicating time to reading helps cultivate discipline and focus. Societies that encourage reading tend to be more informed, empathetic, and innovative. Thus, reading is not merely a pastime but a lifelong tool for personal growth and societal advancement.",
