    "question": "Write a Letter to the Mayor of Aizawl Municipal Corporation highlighting the rising incidence of burglary in various localities of Aizawl city and urging him to implement concrete measures to address the issue, including some remedial suggestions. Sign as XYZ of ABC locality.",
    "explanation": "This is a formal letter to a public authority, so use the full official layout: sender's address (XYZ, ABC Locality, Aizawl, Mizoram) and date; the addressee block 'The Mayor, Aizawl Municipal Corporation, Aizawl, Mizoram'; a subject line ('Sub: Rising incidence of burglary in Aizawl localities — request for remedial measures'); the salutation 'Sir,'; three short body paragraphs; then 'Yours faithfully, XYZ, ABC Locality'. Do NOT sign with your real name — the paper says sign as XYZ of ABC locality, and inventing a name loses marks. Paragraph one states the purpose and who you write as (a resident of ABC locality). Paragraph two gives the substance: burglaries rising across several localities, break-ins during daytime working hours and at night, unlit lanes and blind corners, absent or non-functional street lighting, houses left empty during office hours, and the resulting fear among elderly residents and women living alone. Paragraph three carries the remedial suggestions the question explicitly asks for — restore and extend street lighting on inner lanes, install CCTV at locality entry points and junctions, support and coordinate with local Y.M.A. and Village Council night patrols, request the Mayor to take up increased night beat patrolling with the district police, publish a locality-wise complaint helpline, and clear overgrown vegetation and abandoned structures that give cover. Close by requesting early action and offering the locality's cooperation. Keep the tone respectful and factual, never accusatory, and stay under about 200 words in the body.",
    "guidance": "This is a formal letter to a public authority, so use the full official layout: sender's address (XYZ, ABC Locality, Aizawl, Mizoram) and date; the addressee block 'The Mayor, Aizawl Municipal Corporation, Aizawl, Mizoram'; a subject line ('Sub: Rising incidence of burglary in Aizawl localities — request for remedial measures'); the salutation 'Sir,'; three short body paragraphs; then 'Yours faithfully, XYZ, ABC Locality'. Do NOT sign with your real name — the paper says sign as XYZ of ABC locality, and inventing a name loses marks. Paragraph one states the purpose and who you write as (a resident of ABC locality). Paragraph two gives the substance: burglaries rising across several localities, break-ins during daytime working hours and at night, unlit lanes and blind corners, absent or non-functional street lighting, houses left empty during office hours, and the resulting fear among elderly residents and women living alone. Paragraph three carries the remedial suggestions the question explicitly asks for — restore and extend street lighting on inner lanes, install CCTV at locality entry points and junctions, support and coordinate with local Y.M.A. and Village Council night patrols, request the Mayor to take up increased night beat patrolling with the district police, publish a locality-wise complaint helpline, and clear overgrown vegetation and abandoned structures that give cover. Close by requesting early action and offering the locality's cooperation. Keep the tone respectful and factual, never accusatory, and stay under about 200 words in the body.",
